  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rE00 Site Location Plan 23.06.2025\t\rE01 existing drawings elevations 23.06.2025\rE02 existing drawings elevations 23.06.2025\rE03 existing drawings elevations 23.06.2025\rE04 existing drawings elevations 23.06.2025\rP00 proposed drawings site plans 29.09.2025\rP01 proposed drawings floor plans 29.09.2025\rP02 proposed drawings elevations 29.09.2025\rP03 proposed drawings elevations 29.09.2025\rP04 proposed drawings sections 29.09.2025\rP05 proposed drawings details 29.09.2025\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than six residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority. \r\rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the communal kitchen and dining/living rooms shall be retained in perpetuity. The window of ensuite bathroom to bedrooms 5 and the first floor communal bathroom window shall be fitted with obscure glass or obscure glazed film over the entirety of the glass and be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "Notwithstanding the cycle parking indicated on drawing 'PROPOSED DRAWINGS SITE PLANS P00 29 September 2025', prior to occupation, unless otherwise agreed, cycle parking should be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\r- Provision of a minimum of SIX long stay cycle parking spaces, one per HMO bedroom.\r\r- In an accessible location: The access route to the cycle parking enclosures should be of sufficient wide to enable the bike to enter the store. \r\rSuch facilities to be retained permanently thereafter.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision and availability of adequate cycle parking.\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application. The window of ensuite bathroom to bedrooms 5 and the first floor communal bathroom window shall be fitted with obscure glass or obscure glazed film over the entirety of the glass and be retained in perpetuity.\r \rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r"
  ],
